  "term": "DEX",
  "definition": "DEX refers to dexmedetomidine, a selective alpha-2 adrenergic receptor agonist with sedative effects. In the source, it is discussed as an anesthetic-related drug that has been associated with lower rates of delirium and cognitive decline in older adults, although it is not suitable by itself for general anesthesia.",
